   $q$In the last stanza, what does "holding on a little less" most likely mean beyond flying a kite?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Not trying to control things so tightly can help them go well.","is_correct":true},{"text":"People should drop the things they are carrying in their hands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Giving up on a hard task is better than trying to finish it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-theme"},{"text":"Kite strings should always be cut short so the kite stays low.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Not trying to control things so tightly can help them go well.$q$, $q$The speaker says "Now when I want things fast and right," so the kite lesson now applies to other things in life. The speaker does not give up; the speaker keeps flying the kite in a gentler way.$q$, 'draft', '60380577-c54a-532a-8e39-a499db1f8741')
