   $q$Which is the best summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker is the kindest and hardest working kid in the whole town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Mr. Petrov leaves a jar of cookies and a note on the speaker's porch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The speaker and Mr. Petrov build a snowman beside his front tree.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"After a big snow, the speaker shovels a neighbor's walk, gets a thank-you and soon other kids help too.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After a big snow, the speaker shovels a neighbor's walk, gets a thank-you and soon other kids help too.$q$, $q$This choice covers the storm, the kind act, the thank-you and how the helping spreads. The cookies and note are only the third stanza, so that choice is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', '1b581b42-04f5-5c12-86b9-cbf174f5c5e0')
